Software
--------
The code in this repository is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(see LICENSE).

The archive interface and build tooling are derived from the DEEMO artwork
archive by FridrichMethod, https://github.com/FridrichMethod/deemo, at commit
b14bf0d5f5a05e5382c319f3fd5019a4936820b8 (Apache-2.0). That archive is itself
derived from Mashiro's DEEMO gallery, https://github.com/mashirozx/deemo
(Apache-2.0); the original gallery design is Mashiro's. Only code was
adapted: no artwork, audio, fonts, manifests or other data of either DEEMO
repository are included.

Files adapted in 2026 say so in a notice at their top:
  archive.html, browserconfig.xml, src/archive.css, src/archive.js,
  src/i18n.js, src/i18n/common.js, src/i18n/archive.js and
  src/i18n/slideshow.js (from the DEEMO archive);
  templates/slideshow.html (from the DEEMO archive's template, itself derived
  from mashirozx/deemo test.html; the generated index.html copies its header)
  and src/slideshow.css (from the DEEMO archive, itself derived from
  mashirozx/deemo style.css);
  scripts/build_catalog.py, scripts/build_thumbnails.py and
  scripts/prepare_pages.py (from the same scripts of the DEEMO archive);
  scripts/render_slideshow.py (from the slideshow rendering helpers of the
  DEEMO archive's scripts/build_catalog.py);
  tests/browser_smoke.py, tests/test_archive_labels.py, tests/test_catalog.py,
  tests/test_i18n.py, tests/test_layout.py, tests/test_slideshow.py and
  tests/test_thumbnails.py (from the same tests of the DEEMO archive).
site.webmanifest (JSON, which allows no comments) follows the structure of
the DEEMO archive's manifest with this project's names and icons. Everything
else was written for this project.

Third-party software
--------------------
src/vendor/legacy-ui.js is byte-identical to src/vendor/legacy-ui.js of the
DEEMO archive at the commit above, which is the upstream src/main.js of
mashirozx/deemo. It is used for the slideshow screenshot feature and bundles
software under the MIT License, whose full texts are in licenses/:
  html2canvas 0.5.0-beta3, Copyright (c) 2012 Niklas von Hertzen
    (licenses/html2canvas-MIT.txt; the bundle banner names 2016 and leaves
    the license name blank)
  punycode.js 1.2.4, Copyright Mathias Bynens, built into html2canvas
    (licenses/punycode-MIT.txt)
  Pace 1.0.0, Copyright (c) 2013 HubSpot, Inc. (licenses/pace-MIT.txt)

The icons under assets/site/ were made for this project (see
assets/site/README.md) and are covered by the software license together with
the page code. The pages use system fonts; no font, audio or background image
is distributed.

